{# Gender balance over the life of a series, drawn like the acceptance rates:
   the pooled total first, then one row per year, most recent at the top.

   Expects `rows`, `total`, `label` and `band` from the including template, so
   that the leadership and the programme committee render the same way without
   ever being added together.

   Each bar is three segments. Colour alone says nothing here — every segment
   carries a title, and the counts are written out beside it — because a
   reader who cannot separate the hues must still be able to read the row.

   When the corpus has enough data to have a rate of its own, a hairline is
   drawn across every bar at that rate. It is the same device the acceptance
   chart uses for its 30% line, and it does the work a colour code would do
   less honestly: the reader sees which years fall short of what this field
   actually does, rather than being told. #}
{% macro bar(r) -%}
{%- if r.women %}<i class="g-w" style="--w: {{ (100 * r.women / r.total) | round(2) }}%"
  title="{{ r.women }} of {{ r.total }} women"></i>{% endif %}
{%- if r.other %}<i class="g-o" style="--w: {{ (100 * r.other / r.total) | round(2) }}%"
  title="{{ r.other }} of {{ r.total }} another gender"></i>{% endif %}
{%- if r.men %}<i class="g-m" style="--w: {{ (100 * r.men / r.total) | round(2) }}%"
  title="{{ r.men }} of {{ r.total }} men"></i>{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
<ol class="ratechart genderchart"
    {%- if band %} style="--base: {{ band.rate }}%"{% endif %}>
  <li class="is-total"{% if band %} data-band="{{ band.band }}"{% endif %}>
    <span class="ry">all {{ total.editions }}</span>
    <span class="rb{% if band %} has-base{% endif %}">{{ bar(total) }}</span>
    <span class="rv">{{ total.share }}%<small> of {{ total.total }}</small></span>
  </li>
  {% for r in rows %}
  <li>
    <span class="ry"><a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.year }}</a></span>
    <span class="rb{% if band %} has-base{% endif %}">{{ bar(r) }}</span>
    <span class="rv">{{ r.women + r.other }}<small> of {{ r.total }}</small></span>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>
<p class="chart-caption genderpooled">Across {{ total.editions }} editions,
  <b>{{ total.women + total.other }} of {{ total.total }}</b> {{ label }}
  were women or of another gender &mdash; {{ total.share }}%.
  {%- if band %}
  At this site's own rate of {{ band.rate }}%, {{ band.expected }} would be the
  expectation.
  {%- if band.none and band.unlikely %}
  <b>Not one of the {{ total.total }} was.</b> A platform this size drawn at
  that rate would be all men less than once in twenty times.
  {%- elif band.unlikely %}
  A shortfall this large would happen by chance less than once in twenty times.
  {%- elif band.below %}
  The gap is within what chance would produce at these numbers.
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}</p>
